    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation says the low-resolution image becomes a dense feature field, then windows are taken from that field.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder acts on the low-resolution image, not on already formed windows. Its output is the dense feature field named F. The window operator is applied to that field. The tokens are partitioned into X, so the carrier remains the source of every window token.",
